No, I call pendingTasks from a third thread which is used to monitor netty status. The code is as following: 

```
public class NettyEventLoopGroupMonitor implements StatisticItem {
    EventLoopGroup group;
    public NettyEventLoopGroupMonitor(EventLoopGroup group)
    {
        this.group = group;
    }

    @Override
    public void saveAndReset(String name, Map<String, Object> output) {
        Set<EventExecutor> executors = group.children();
        int tasks = 0;
        for (EventExecutor executor: executors)
        {
            if (executor instanceof SingleThreadEventExecutor) {
                SingleThreadEventExecutor e = (SingleThreadEventExecutor) executor;
                tasks += e.pendingTasks();

            }

        }

        output.put("netty_" + name, tasks);
    }
}
```
